// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Sysmon Driver Altitude Change
// Sigma ID: 4916a35e-bfc4-47d0-8e25-a003d7067061
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: B.Talebi
// Date: 2022-07-28 | Modified: 2026-11-16
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects changes in Sysmon driver altitude value. If the Sysmon driver is configured to load at
//   an altitude of another registered service, it will fail to load at boot.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate driver altitude change to hide sysmon
// References:
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/shhmon-silencing-sysmon-via-driver-unload-682b5be57650
//   - https://youtu.be/zSihR3lTf7g
//   - https://github.com/trustedsec/SysmonCommunityGuide/blob/557dbd51b98952bc26f698620e48dfc7833b5cf0/chapters/the-sysmon-driver.md
//   - https://medium.com/@matterpreter/shhmon-silencing-sysmon-via-driver-unload-682b5be57650
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7450e84bf4fd4980968034ff175230b60063676b/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_change_sysmon_driver_altitude.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Services.*$" and RegistryKey endswith "\\Instances\\Sysmon Instance\\Altitude") and (not(RegistryValueData == 385201))
